{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "DAN",
  "chapter": 8,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "DAN.8.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:DAN.8.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "In the third year of the reign of king Belshazzar a vision appeared to me, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "even to",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " me, Daniel, after that which appeared to me at the first.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "DAN.8.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:DAN.8.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And I saw in a vision; and it came to pass, when I saw, that I ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "was",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " at Shushan ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "in",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the palace, which ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " in the province of Elam; and I saw in a vision, and I was by the river Ulai.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "DAN.8.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:DAN.8.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then I lifted up my eyes, and saw, and behold, there stood before the river a ram which had ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "two",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " horns: and the ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "two",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " horns ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "were",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " high; but one ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "was",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " higher than the other, and the higher came up last.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "DAN.8.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:DAN.8.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I saw the ram pushing westward, and northward, and southward; so that no beasts might stand before him, neither ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "was there any",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " that could deliver out of his hand; but he did according to his will, and became great.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "DAN.8.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:DAN.8.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And as I was considering, behold, a he-goat came from the west on the face of the whole earth, and touched not the ground: and the goat ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "had",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " a notable horn between his eyes.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "DAN.8.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:DAN.8.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And he came to the ram that had ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "two",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " horns, which I had seen standing before the river, and ran to him in the fury of his power.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "DAN.8.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:DAN.8.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And I saw him come close to the ram, and he was moved with anger against him, and smote the ram, and broke his two horns: and there was no power in the ram to stand before him, but he cast him down to the ground, and stamped upon him: and there was none that could deliver the ram out of his hand.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "DAN.8.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:DAN.8.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Therefore the he-goat became very great: and when he was strong, the great horn was broken; and in its stead came up four notable ones towards the four winds of heaven.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "DAN.8.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:DAN.8.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And out of one of them came forth a little horn, which became exceeding great, towards the south, and towards the east, and towards the pleasant ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "land",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ".",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "DAN.8.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:DAN.8.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And it grew great, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "even",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " to the host of heaven; and it cast down ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "some",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " of the host and of the stars to the ground, and stamped upon them.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "DAN.8.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:DAN.8.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Yes, he magnified ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "himself",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " even to the prince of the host, and by him the daily ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "sacrifice",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " was taken away, and the place of his sanctuary was cast down.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "DAN.8.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:DAN.8.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And a host was given ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "him",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " against the daily ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "sacrifice",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " by reason of transgression, and it cast down the truth to the ground; and it practiced, and prospered.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "DAN.8.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:DAN.8.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Then I heard one saint speaking, and another saint said to that certain ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "saint",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " who spoke, How long ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "shall be",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the vision ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "concerning",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the daily ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "sacrifice",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", and the transgression of desolation, to give both the sanctuary and the host to be trodden under foot?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "DAN.8.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:DAN.8.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And he said to me, Until two thousand and three hundred days; then shall the sanctuary be cleansed.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "DAN.8.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:DAN.8.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And it came to pass, when I, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "even",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " I Daniel, had seen the vision, and sought for the meaning, then behold, there stood before me as the appearance of a man.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "DAN.8.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:DAN.8.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And I heard a man's voice between ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "the banks of",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " Ulai, which called, and said, Gabriel, make this ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "man",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " to understand the vision.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "DAN.8.17",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:DAN.8.17",
      "verse": 17,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "So he came near where I stood: and when he came, I was afraid, and fell upon my face: but he said to me, Understand, O son of man: for at the time of the end ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "shall be",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the vision.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "DAN.8.18",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:DAN.8.18",
      "verse": 18,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Now as he was speaking with me, I was in a deep sleep on my face towards the ground: but he touched me, and set me upright.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "DAN.8.19",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:DAN.8.19",
      "verse": 19,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And he said, Behold, I will make thee know what shall be in the last end of the indignation: for at the time appointed the end ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "shall be",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ".",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "DAN.8.20",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:DAN.8.20",
      "verse": 20,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The ram which thou sawest having ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "two",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " horns ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "are",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the kings of Media and Persia.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "DAN.8.21",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:DAN.8.21",
      "verse": 21,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And the rough goat ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the king of Grecia: and the great horn that ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " between his eyes ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the first king.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "DAN.8.22",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:DAN.8.22",
      "verse": 22,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Now that being broken, whereas four stood up in its place, four kingdoms shall stand up out of the nation, but not in his power.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "DAN.8.23",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:DAN.8.23",
      "verse": 23,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And in the latter time of their kingdom, when the transgressors are come to the full, a king of fierce countenance, and understanding dark sentences, shall stand up.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "DAN.8.24",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:DAN.8.24",
      "verse": 24,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And his power shall be mighty, but not by his own power: and he shall destroy wonderfully, and shall prosper, and practice, and shall destroy the mighty and the holy people.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "DAN.8.25",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:DAN.8.25",
      "verse": 25,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And through his policy also he shall cause craft to prosper in his hand; and he shall magnify ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "himself",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " in his heart, and by peace shall destroy many: he shall also stand up against the Prince of princes; but he shall be broken without hand.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "DAN.8.26",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:DAN.8.26",
      "verse": 26,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And the vision of the evening and the morning which was told ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " true: wherefore shut thou up the vision; for it ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "shall be",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " for many days.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "DAN.8.27",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:DAN.8.27",
      "verse": 27,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And I Daniel fainted, and was sick ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "certain",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " days; afterward I rose, and did the king's business; and I was astonished at the vision, but none understood ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "it",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ".",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
